[{"code":"pipe_rhs_not_application","severity":"error","span":{"file":"tests/corpus/parse/bad/PipeRhsNotApplication.beni","start":{"line":8,"col":11},"end":{"line":8,"col":13}},"title":"PIPE WITHOUT A CALL","message":"I was expecting a call after this `|>`, but I ran into `λ`.\n\n`x |> f a` is `f x a`: the value on the left becomes the FIRST argument of the\ncall on the right, so the right of `|>` must be that call — a function, or a\ncall it is one argument short of. A `let`, `if`, `case` or lambda has no\nargument list to insert into. Parentheses do not hand it over as a value either\n— they are looked through, so `5 |> (\\y -> y + 1)` CALLS the lambda on `5` and\nis `6`. Write that if it is what you meant. When the block is the argument\nrather than the function, it belongs on the right of `<|`, which does carry one:\n`f a <| case x of ...`."},{"code":"pipe_rhs_not_application","severity":"error","span":{"file":"tests/corpus/parse/bad/PipeRhsNotApplication.beni","start":{"line":12,"col":10},"end":{"line":12,"col":12}},"title":"PIPE WITHOUT A CALL","message":"I was expecting a call after this `|>`, but I ran into `if`.\n\n`x |> f a` is `f x a`: the value on the left becomes the FIRST argument of the\ncall on the right, so the right of `|>` must be that call — a function, or a\ncall it is one argument short of. A `let`, `if`, `case` or lambda has no\nargument list to insert into. Parentheses do not hand it over as a value either\n— they are looked through, so `5 |> (\\y -> y + 1)` CALLS the lambda on `5` and\nis `6`. Write that if it is what you meant. When the block is the argument\nrather than the function, it belongs on the right of `<|`, which does carry one:\n`f a <| case x of ...`."},{"code":"pipe_rhs_not_application","severity":"error","span":{"file":"tests/corpus/parse/bad/PipeRhsNotApplication.beni","start":{"line":16,"col":10},"end":{"line":16,"col":14}},"title":"PIPE WITHOUT A CALL","message":"I was expecting a call after this `|>`, but I ran into `case`.\n\n`x |> f a` is `f x a`: the value on the left becomes the FIRST argument of the\ncall on the right, so the right of `|>` must be that call — a function, or a\ncall it is one argument short of. A `let`, `if`, `case` or lambda has no\nargument list to insert into. Parentheses do not hand it over as a value either\n— they are looked through, so `5 |> (\\y -> y + 1)` CALLS the lambda on `5` and\nis `6`. Write that if it is what you meant. When the block is the argument\nrather than the function, it belongs on the right of `<|`, which does carry one:\n`f a <| case x of ...`."},{"code":"pipe_rhs_not_application","severity":"error","span":{"file":"tests/corpus/parse/bad/PipeRhsNotApplication.beni","start":{"line":26,"col":12},"end":{"line":26,"col":15}},"title":"PIPE WITHOUT A CALL","message":"I was expecting a call after this `|>`, but I ran into `let`.\n\n`x |> f a` is `f x a`: the value on the left becomes the FIRST argument of the\ncall on the right, so the right of `|>` must be that call — a function, or a\ncall it is one argument short of. A `let`, `if`, `case` or lambda has no\nargument list to insert into. Parentheses do not hand it over as a value either\n— they are looked through, so `5 |> (\\y -> y + 1)` CALLS the lambda on `5` and\nis `6`. Write that if it is what you meant. When the block is the argument\nrather than the function, it belongs on the right of `<|`, which does carry one:\n`f a <| case x of ...`."},{"code":"pipe_rhs_not_application","severity":"error","span":{"file":"tests/corpus/parse/bad/PipeRhsNotApplication.beni","start":{"line":34,"col":14},"end":{"line":34,"col":15}},"title":"PIPE WITHOUT A CALL","message":"I was expecting a call after this `|>`, but I ran into `+`.\n\n`x |> f a` is `f x a`: the value on the left becomes the FIRST argument of the\ncall on the right, so the right of `|>` must be that call — a function, or a\ncall it is one argument short of. A `let`, `if`, `case` or lambda has no\nargument list to insert into. Parentheses do not hand it over as a value either\n— they are looked through, so `5 |> (\\y -> y + 1)` CALLS the lambda on `5` and\nis `6`. Write that if it is what you meant. When the block is the argument\nrather than the function, it belongs on the right of `<|`, which does carry one:\n`f a <| case x of ...`."},{"code":"pipe_rhs_not_application","severity":"error","span":{"file":"tests/corpus/parse/bad/PipeRhsNotApplication.beni","start":{"line":38,"col":13},"end":{"line":38,"col":14}},"title":"PIPE WITHOUT A CALL","message":"I was expecting a call after this `|>`, but I ran into `?`.\n\n`x |> f a` is `f x a`: the value on the left becomes the FIRST argument of the\ncall on the right, so the right of `|>` must be that call — a function, or a\ncall it is one argument short of. A `let`, `if`, `case` or lambda has no\nargument list to insert into. Parentheses do not hand it over as a value either\n— they are looked through, so `5 |> (\\y -> y + 1)` CALLS the lambda on `5` and\nis `6`. Write that if it is what you meant. When the block is the argument\nrather than the function, it belongs on the right of `<|`, which does carry one:\n`f a <| case x of ...`."}]
